EUROPEAN COURT OF HUMAN RIGHTS

CASE OF LUNDBERG AND OTHERS v. THE KINGDOM OF NORDICA

(Application No. 54321/20)

JUDGMENT

(Strasbourg, 1 April 2023)

The European Court of Human Rights, sitting as a Chamber composed of:

Judge Sofia Ivanova,
Judge Lars Andersson,
Judge Elena Petrov,
Judge Henrik Jensen,
Judge Anna Kowalski,
Judge Alessia Rossi,
Judge Miguel Fernandez,

Having regard to the above-mentioned case brought before the Court by Lundberg and Others against the Kingdom of Nordica;

Having regard to the application alleging violations of Articles 9, 10, 11, and 14 of the Convention for the Protection of Human Rights and Fundamental Freedoms and Article 1 of Protocol No. 1;

Having regard to the applicants' status as five Swedish nationals employed by a construction company bound by a collective labor agreement, and their claim that the monitoring fees on their wages constituted a violation of their rights;

Having held a public hearing in Strasbourg to address the admissibility of the application for the individual applicants and the Industries;

Considering the arguments presented by both the applicants and the Government of the Kingdom of Nordica;

Having examined the alleged violations in light of the relevant Convention articles and legal principles;

The Court hereby:

1. Declares the application admissible for the individual applicants;

2. Declares the application inadmissible for the Industries;

3. Reserves the judgment on the alleged violations for further deliberation.

Done in English and notified in writing on this 1st day of April 2023.

Sofia Ivanova
President
